{"id":"diclazepam","name":"Diclazepam","form":"tablet","status":"Well-documented","aliases":"","category":"Depressant","chemicalClass":"Benzodiazepines","psychoactiveClass":"Depressant","addictionPotential":"extremely physically and psychologically addictive","toxicity":["low toxicity","potentially lethal when mixed with depressants like alcohol or opioids"],"summarySources":"PsychonautWiki, TripSit","summary":"A benzodiazepine drug and analogue of diazepam first synthesised by Leo Sternbach at Hoffman-LaRoche in 1960. It has become prominent as an RC benzodiazepine on the grey market in recent years, particularly with the decline in etizolam availability. A sedative and hypnotic it is of intermediate to long half-life with similar effects to diazepam, though it is 10x more potent.","advisory":"Potentially lethal when mixed with depressants like alcohol or opioids.","doseMaxTick":8,"doseUnit":"mg","doseRows":[{"roa":"Oral","source":"PsychonautWiki","unit":"mg","threshold":"0.5 mg","light":"0.5–1 mg","common":"1–3 mg","strong":"3–4 mg","heavy":"4 mg+","commonEstimate":2,"band":{"low":1,"high":3},"domain":[0.4,6.6],"segments":{"light":[0.5,1],"common":[1,3],"strong":[3,4],"heavy":[4,6.34]}}],"durationSources":"PsychonautWiki, TripSit","durationRows":[{"roa":"Oral","onset":"10–45 min","comeup":"—","peak":"—","offset":"—","afterEffects":"—","total":"8–12 h"}],"tolerance":{"buildUp":"within 3-4 days of continuous use","reset":"7 - 14 days","milestones":[{"label":"Full tolerance","value":"within 3-4 days of continuous use","tone":"danger"},{"label":"Baseline","value":"7 - 14 days","tone":"positive"}],"crossTolerances":[{"group":"Cross-tolerance","items":["GABAergic"]}]},"subjectiveEffects":[{"name":"Amnesia","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Amnesia"},{"name":"Analysis suppression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Analysis_suppression"},{"name":"Anxiety suppression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Anxiety_suppression"},{"name":"Compulsive redosing","url"